-- title:
--   Cumulative budget minima and tree tolerances
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $e$ assign positive budgets to the nonroot nodes of an ordered tree.
--
--   1. **Level minimum.** The minimum of $e$ over the nodes at depth $k+1$, which is nonempty.
--   2. **Cumulative minimum.** $m_0=1$ and $m_{k+1}=\min(m_k,\text{level minimum at }k+1)$. So $a\le m_k$ iff $a\le1$ and $a$ is below every budget at depths $1,\dots,k$.
--   3. **Tolerance.**
--   $$
--   \tau_k=2^{-(k+1)}m_k ,
--   $$
--   with $\tau_0=\frac12$. Every finite tail $\sum_{d\ge k}\tau_d$ is bounded by every budget at depth at most $k$.
